# serializer version: 1
# name: test_answer_publish_golden
  '''
  role: standalone
  params:
    runActivity: "run-claude"
    agentId: "claude-agent"
  steps:
    - id: answer
      activity: "{{params.runActivity}}"
      input:
        outputContract: {"properties":{"answer":{"description":"the conclusive answer to the task, plainly stated","type":"string"},"disagreements":{"description":"panel runs only — where independent answers diverged and why it matters; empty or omitted otherwise","type":"string"}},"required":["answer"],"type":"object"}
        task: |-
          Answer the task under ===TASK=== below. Work independently from your own knowledge and
          reasoning; do not ask questions. Be concise and conclusive — end with your answer,
          plainly stated, reported via the fields of your final json block.
          
          ===OUTPUT CONTRACT===
          End your final message with a fenced ```json code block containing a single JSON
          object matching this schema. The block is machine-validated: a missing or
          mismatching block fails this step. Nothing may follow the block.
          {
            "properties": {
              "answer": {
                "description": "the conclusive answer to the task, plainly stated",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "disagreements": {
                "description": "panel runs only — where independent answers diverged and why it matters; empty or omitted otherwise",
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "answer"
            ],
            "type": "object"
          }
  
          ===TASK===
          {{params.task}}
  outputs:
    type: object
    required:
      - answer
    properties:
      answer:
        type: string
        description: the conclusive answer to the task, plainly stated
      disagreements:
        type: string
        description: >-
          panel runs only — where independent answers diverged and why it matters; empty or
          omitted otherwise
  panelSynthesis: |-
    Merge the panelists' answers into ONE conclusive `answer`: prefer the strongest reasoning
    over the largest headcount, and merge complementary points rather than picking a side when
    they compose. Surface real divergences — different conclusions, not different phrasings —
    in `disagreements`, naming which panelist held what and why it matters; leave it empty
    when the panel genuinely agrees.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_arm_revise_golden
  '''
  role: overlay
  steps:
    - id: arm-revise-pr
      activity: register-cron
      input:
        # The saved workflow the cron re-fires each due tick until the PR merges (revise reports
        # a structured `goal: RESOLVED` on merge; the cron engine reads wf:*.resolved and deactivates).
        workflow: revise-pr
        repo: "{{params.repo}}"
        slug: "{{params.slug}}"
        cadence: "0 */6 * * *"
        maxFires: 20
        # Only arm if the PR actually opened: register-cron reads the `pr` field of create-pr's output json block.
        requirePrFrom: "{{create-pr.output}}"
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_bootstrap_repo_publish_golden
  '''
  role: standalone
  params:
    runActivity: "run-claude"
    agentId: "claude-agent"
    visibility: "private"
  steps:
    - id: setup
      activity: setup
      input:
        agentId: "{{params.agentId}}"
        setup:
          - cmd: "mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -rn \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/. ~/.claude/skills/"
          - cmd: "if [ -f $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md ]; then bash \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/install-steering.sh $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md; fi"
          - cmd: "bash ~/.claude/skills/install-plugins.sh \"{{params.plugins}}\" https://github.com/stiproot/hex-arch https://github.com/stiproot/plan-management https://github.com/stiproot/code-comprehension"
    - id: bootstrap
      activity: "{{params.runActivity}}"
      input:
        outputContract: {"properties":{"defaultBranch":{"description":"the default branch name (main) (required on CREATED, omitted on FAILED)","type":"string"},"repoUrl":{"description":"the HTML URL of the created repository (required on CREATED, omitted on FAILED)","type":"string"},"result":{"description":"CREATED when the repository was created, committed, and pushed; FAILED otherwise","enum":["CREATED","FAILED"]},"skipped":{"description":"present on FAILED — why the run halted (repo already exists, gate failure, GH_TOKEN unset, verifyCmd not provided, ...)","type":"string"},"verify":{"description":"the acceptance-gate outcome; PASS only when gate ran and passed; omitted if gate was skipped","enum":["PASS","FAIL"]}},"required":["result"],"type":"object"}
        task: |-
          Your job is to create a new GitHub repository named {{params.repoName}} and bootstrap it
          from the spec below. Work in your current directory (the agent workspace). There is no
          pre-cloned repo — you are building from scratch.
  
          ===SPEC===
          {{params.spec}}
  
          Follow this procedure exactly, in order. Stop immediately on any failure and report via
          the final json block.
  
          1. CREATE the repository.
             Use the github MCP tool create_repository:
               name: {{params.repoName}}
               visibility: {{params.visibility}}
             Set the tool's `private` parameter to true when the visibility value above is
             "private" (or empty), and to false only when it is exactly "public".
             If the repository already exists (the tool returns an error indicating the name is
             taken), STOP. Report `result: FAILED` and `skipped: "repo already exists"`. Do not
             adopt, modify, or push to an existing repository.
             On success: note the returned `html_url` as `repoUrl` and the `default_branch` as
             `defaultBranch` for your final json block.
  
          2. SCAFFOLD the project.
             In your current working directory:
               git init
             Implement the project as described under ===SPEC=== above. Create all files needed to
             satisfy the spec. Do not create files outside the spec.
  
          3. VERIFY.
             If verifyCmd is empty or not provided, STOP. Report `result: FAILED` and
             `skipped: "verifyCmd not provided"`. Do not proceed without a verification gate.
             Otherwise, run the acceptance command exactly as given (no modifications, no weakening):
               {{params.verifyCmd}}
             If it fails, fix forward and retry up to 3 times. If it still fails after 3 attempts,
             STOP. Report `result: FAILED`, `verify: FAIL`, and `skipped: "verify gate failed after
             3 attempts"`. Do not push a repository that does not pass the gate.
             On success: note `verify: PASS` for your final json block.
  
          4. COMMIT and PUSH.
             Stage and commit files individually (never `git add -A` or `git commit -a`):
               git add <file>   # repeat for each file
             Use a single conventional commit message summarising the scaffold.
             Set the default branch:
               git branch -M main
             Push with a one-shot token URL — extract <owner> SAFELY from the creation response or
             your GitHub username. The owner must be URL-safe; if extracting from `git remote get-url origin`,
             extract the segment between github.com/ and the repo name, e.g. from
             https://github.com/octocat/repo.git → octocat. Do not include special characters or slashes.
             The repo name is {{params.repoName}}:
               git remote add origin "https://github.com/<owner>/{{params.repoName}}.git"
               git push "https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/<owner>/{{params.repoName}}.git" main
             Never write the token into git config or the remote URL permanently.
             If GH_TOKEN is unset, STOP. Report `result: FAILED` and
             `skipped: "GH_TOKEN is not set"`.
  
          Report the outcome ONLY via the fields of your final json block below. There is no other
          reporting channel.
          
          ===OUTPUT CONTRACT===
          End your final message with a fenced ```json code block containing a single JSON
          object matching this schema. The block is machine-validated: a missing or
          mismatching block fails this step. Nothing may follow the block.
          {
            "properties": {
              "defaultBranch": {
                "description": "the default branch name (main) (required on CREATED, omitted on FAILED)",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "repoUrl": {
                "description": "the HTML URL of the created repository (required on CREATED, omitted on FAILED)",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "result": {
                "description": "CREATED when the repository was created, committed, and pushed; FAILED otherwise",
                "enum": [
                  "CREATED",
                  "FAILED"
                ]
              },
              "skipped": {
                "description": "present on FAILED — why the run halted (repo already exists, gate failure, GH_TOKEN unset, verifyCmd not provided, ...)",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "verify": {
                "description": "the acceptance-gate outcome; PASS only when gate ran and passed; omitted if gate was skipped",
                "enum": [
                  "PASS",
                  "FAIL"
                ]
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "result"
            ],
            "type": "object"
          }
  outputs:
    type: object
    required:
      - result
    properties:
      result:
        enum:
          - CREATED
          - FAILED
        description: CREATED when the repository was created, committed, and pushed; FAILED otherwise
      repoUrl:
        type: string
        description: the HTML URL of the created repository (required on CREATED, omitted on FAILED)
      defaultBranch:
        type: string
        description: the default branch name (main) (required on CREATED, omitted on FAILED)
      verify:
        enum:
          - PASS
          - FAIL
        description: the acceptance-gate outcome; PASS only when gate ran and passed; omitted if gate was skipped
      skipped:
        type: string
        description: present on FAILED — why the run halted (repo already exists, gate failure, GH_TOKEN unset, verifyCmd not provided, ...)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_create_pr_golden
  '''
  role: overlay
  params:
    issueNumber: ""
  steps:
    - id: create-pr
      activity: "{{params.runActivity}}"
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "{{params.modelImplement}}"
        outputContract: {"properties":{"pr":{"description":"the pull request number, when a PR exists (opened, updated, or pre-existing)","type":"integer"},"skipped":{"description":"present INSTEAD of pr/url — why no PR exists (verify gate failed, auth failure, nothing to push, ...)","type":"string"},"url":{"description":"the pull request URL","type":"string"}},"type":"object"}
        task: |-
          ===ISSUE===
          {{params.issueNumber}}
  
          The implementation step has committed the changes locally on branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
          Read plan-feature-{{params.slug}}.md in the worktree root and the local commit on
          feature/{{params.slug}} to understand what the implementation step did — use these as your
          sources for the PR title and body. Now push and open (or update) a pull request.
          1. Push the branch. The origin remote has no credentials — derive <owner>/<repo>
             from `git remote get-url origin` and push with a one-shot token URL:
             git push "https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git" feature/{{params.slug}}
             Never write the token into git config or the remote URL; if GH_TOKEN is unset,
             skip the push and explain why in the `skipped` field of your final json block.
          2. Open a pull request against the repository's default branch with the github
             MCP tool create_pull_request: title from the feature, body from the plan file
             and the implementation commit (summarize what the implementation step committed).
             Include the `===ITEST EVIDENCE===` section below in the PR body when those values
             are non-empty (i.e. when run-itest was composed in and ran).
             Pass the intended Markdown directly as the tool's body value, beginning with the intended heading or first line;
             do not wrap it in shell command substitution or a heredoc.
             If the value under ===ISSUE=== above is a number N, include the line
             `Closes #N` on its own line in the PR body, so the merge auto-closes that issue;
             otherwise omit it. If a PR for this branch already exists, your push has updated
             it — do not open a duplicate.
  
          ===ITEST EVIDENCE===
          class: {{itest.class}}
          treeHash: {{itest.treeHash}}
          durationMs: {{itest.durationMs}}
          outputTail: {{itest.outputTail}}
          Include this evidence section in the PR body only when these values are non-empty
          (itest was composed in and ran).
  
          3. If a PR for this branch already existed before this push (this is a revise
             run, not a first-time creation), respond to review feedback:
             a. Find the PR number: use the github MCP tool to list pull requests by
               head branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
             b. Fetch UNRESOLVED review threads: pull_request_read with method
               get_review_comments on that PR. Each thread has an isResolved field, a
               thread node id (PRRT_...), and comments with numeric ids.
             c. For each unresolved thread that this run actually addressed, reply inline
               with add_reply_to_pull_request_comment (body: "Addressed in <sha>:
               <what changed>"), then resolve it with pull_request_review_write method
               resolve_thread passing the thread node id.
             d. Do NOT reply to or resolve threads this run did not address.
             e. Never APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES on the PR.
          Report the PR (number + URL) — or why it was skipped — ONLY via the fields of
          your final json block below; there is no other reporting channel.
          
          ===OUTPUT CONTRACT===
          End your final message with a fenced ```json code block containing a single JSON
          object matching this schema. The block is machine-validated: a missing or
          mismatching block fails this step. Nothing may follow the block.
          {
            "properties": {
              "pr": {
                "description": "the pull request number, when a PR exists (opened, updated, or pre-existing)",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "skipped": {
                "description": "present INSTEAD of pr/url — why no PR exists (verify gate failed, auth failure, nothing to push, ...)",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "url": {
                "description": "the pull request URL",
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "type": "object"
          }
  outputs:
    type: object
    properties:
      pr:
        type: integer
        description: the pull request number, when a PR exists (opened, updated, or pre-existing)
      url:
        type: string
        description: the pull request URL
      skipped:
        type: string
        description: present INSTEAD of pr/url — why no PR exists (verify gate failed, auth failure, nothing to push, ...)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_gc_worktrees_golden
  '''
  role: standalone
  params:
    agentId: "claude-agent"
    pruneUntracked: "false"
    minAgeMs: "86400000"
    keep: ""
    dryRun: "false"
  steps:
    - id: gc
      activity: gc-worktrees
      input:
        agentId: "{{params.agentId}}"
        pruneUntracked: "{{params.pruneUntracked}}"
        minAgeMs: "{{params.minAgeMs}}"
        keep: "{{params.keep}}"
        dryRun: "{{params.dryRun}}"
        traceparent: "{{traceparent}}"
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_implement_publish_mode_golden
  '''
  role: base
  params:
    runActivity: "run-claude"
    clonePath: ""
    agentId: "claude-agent"
    modelPlan: "claude-sonnet-4-6"
    modelImplement: "claude-haiku-4-5"
  steps:
    - id: worktree
      activity: create-worktree
      input:
        agentId: "{{params.agentId}}"
        clonePath: "{{params.clonePath}}"
        checkout:
          kind: branch
          branch: "feature/{{params.slug}}"
    - id: setup
      activity: setup
      input:
        agentId: "{{params.agentId}}"
        setup:
          - cmd: "mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -rn \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/. ~/.claude/skills/"
          - cmd: "if [ -f $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md ]; then bash \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/install-steering.sh $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md; fi"
    - id: plan
      activity: "{{params.runActivity}}"
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "{{params.modelPlan}}"
        permissionMode: plan
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
  
          First check for a persisted plan from a prior run: if plan-feature-{{params.slug}}.md
          exists in the worktree root, read it — if it still matches the spec and the code,
          reuse it as your plan instead of re-investigating.
  
          Otherwise investigate the feature request under ===FEATURE SPEC=== below: explore the
          relevant code and produce an implementation plan. Do NOT write code or modify any
          files. If the feature already appears implemented, say so in the plan.
          End your response with the plan under the exact marker ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN===.
  
          ===FEATURE SPEC===
          {{params.spec}}
    - id: implement
      activity: "{{params.runActivity}}"
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "{{params.modelImplement}}"
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
  
          First persist the plan you were handed under ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN=== (the
          shared-context handoff, so a re-run or another session can pick it up — the planning
          agent runs read-only and cannot write it itself):
          1. Write it to plan-feature-{{params.slug}}.md in the worktree root. This is the handoff
             and it is required.
          2. ONLY if the dapr MCP is wired in this environment, ALSO call actor_state_set with
             actorId 'feature-{{params.slug}}' and key 'plan', value the plan text — durable in the
             state store, inspectable from another session via actor_state_get. On the LOCAL
             substrate there are no services and so no dapr MCP: the file from (1) sits on the
             operator's own disk and is the whole handoff there, so skipping this is EXPECTED,
             not a degradation — do not attempt the call and do not report its absence.
          If (1) fails, or (2) fails while the tool IS present, do NOT fail the run — but you
          MUST say so explicitly in your final output, so a real degradation stays visible.
  
          Then implement the feature described under ===FEATURE SPEC=== below, following the
          plan. If the feature already appears implemented, make no changes and say so.
          Leave the result as uncommitted working-tree changes — do not commit or push.
  
          ===FEATURE SPEC===
          {{params.spec}}
  
          ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN===
          {{plan.output}}
  
  '''
# ---
