# name: test_implement_yaml_golden
  '''
  role: base
  instanceId: "feature-hostile-fixture"
  steps:
    - id: worktree
      activity: create-worktree
      input:
        agentId: "claude-agent"
        clonePath: "{{params.clonePath}}"
        checkout:
          kind: branch
          branch: "feature/hostile-fixture"
    - id: setup
      activity: setup
      input:
        agentId: "claude-agent"
        setup:
          - cmd: "mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -rn \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/. ~/.claude/skills/"
          - cmd: "if [ -f $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md ]; then bash \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/install-steering.sh $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md; fi"
    - id: plan
      activity: run-claude
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "claude-sonnet-4-6"
        permissionMode: plan
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/hostile-fixture.
  
          First check for a persisted plan from a prior run: if plan-feature-hostile-fixture.md
          exists in the worktree root, read it — if it still matches the spec and the code,
          reuse it as your plan instead of re-investigating.
  
          Otherwise investigate the feature request under ===FEATURE SPEC=== below: explore the
          relevant code and produce an implementation plan. Do NOT write code or modify any
          files. If the feature already appears implemented, say so in the plan.
          End your response with the plan under the exact marker ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN===.
  
          ===FEATURE SPEC===
          # Hostile-content fixture
          
          This spec deliberately carries every token class that must survive rendering untouched.
          It is the committed proof of the delimiter-coexistence story — if any layer (helm, YAML,
          the JSON wire step) mangles one of these, the golden snapshot diff catches it.
          
          - agent-side shell vars: $AGENT_APP_DIR and ${H_SKILLS_DIR}
          - envsubst-style tokens: ${VARS} and ${NOT_A_REAL_VAR}
          - engine-style tokens: {{step.field}} and {"$ref": "step.field"}
          - "double quotes", 'single quotes', back\slashes, a lone $ sign
          - markdown: `inline code`, **bold**, a [link](https://example.invalid)
          
            an indented block
              a deeper one
          
          Trailing punctuation and unicode: café, emoji ✅, em-dash —
          
    - id: implement
      activity: run-claude
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "claude-haiku-4-5"
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/hostile-fixture.
  
          First persist the plan you were handed under ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN=== (the
          shared-context handoff, so a re-run or another session can pick it up — the planning
          agent runs read-only and cannot write it itself):
          1. Write it to plan-feature-hostile-fixture.md in the worktree root. This is the handoff
             and it is required.
          2. ONLY if the dapr MCP is wired in this environment, ALSO call actor_state_set with
             actorId 'feature-hostile-fixture' and key 'plan', value the plan text — durable in the
             state store, inspectable from another session via actor_state_get. On the LOCAL
             substrate there are no services and so no dapr MCP: the file from (1) sits on the
             operator's own disk and is the whole handoff there, so skipping this is EXPECTED,
             not a degradation — do not attempt the call and do not report its absence.
          If (1) fails, or (2) fails while the tool IS present, do NOT fail the run — but you
          MUST say so explicitly in your final output, so a real degradation stays visible.
  
          Then implement the feature described under ===FEATURE SPEC=== below, following the
          plan. If the feature already appears implemented, make no changes and say so.
          Leave the result as uncommitted working-tree changes — do not commit or push.
  
          ===FEATURE SPEC===
          # Hostile-content fixture
          
          This spec deliberately carries every token class that must survive rendering untouched.
          It is the committed proof of the delimiter-coexistence story — if any layer (helm, YAML,
          the JSON wire step) mangles one of these, the golden snapshot diff catches it.
          
          - agent-side shell vars: $AGENT_APP_DIR and ${H_SKILLS_DIR}
          - envsubst-style tokens: ${VARS} and ${NOT_A_REAL_VAR}
          - engine-style tokens: {{step.field}} and {"$ref": "step.field"}
          - "double quotes", 'single quotes', back\slashes, a lone $ sign
          - markdown: `inline code`, **bold**, a [link](https://example.invalid)
          
            an indented block
              a deeper one
          
          Trailing punctuation and unicode: café, emoji ✅, em-dash —
          
  
          ===IMPLEMENTATION PLAN===
          {{plan.output}}
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_improve_plugin_golden
  '''
  role: standalone
  steps:
    - id: worktree
      activity: create-worktree
      input:
        agentId: "claude-agent"
        clonePath: "/workspace/plugins-repo"
        checkout:
          kind: branch
          branch: "improve/{{params.slug}}"
    - id: setup
      activity: setup
      input:
        agentId: "claude-agent"
        setup:
          - cmd: "mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -rn \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/. ~/.claude/skills/"
          - cmd: "if [ -f $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md ]; then bash \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/install-steering.sh $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md; fi"
    - id: improve
      activity: run-claude
      input:
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the plugin repository (your current directory), on branch
          improve/{{params.slug}}. Trace the current linear plugin
          source under plugins/linear (SKILL.md, references/, scripts/) before editing — the
          installed copy can lag the source. Apply the improvement under ===FEEDBACK=== below:
          make a focused change to the plugin source and bump the version in
          plugins/linear/.tessl-plugin/plugin.json. Do not commit or push. Summarize what you
          changed.
  
          ===FEEDBACK===
          {{params.feedback}}
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_plan_publish_golden
  '''
  role: standalone
  params:
    runActivity: "run-claude"
    clonePath: ""
    agentId: "claude-agent"
    modelPlan: "claude-sonnet-4-6"
  steps:
    - id: worktree
      activity: create-worktree
      input:
        agentId: "{{params.agentId}}"
        clonePath: "{{params.clonePath}}"
        checkout:
          kind: branch
          branch: "feature/{{params.slug}}"
    - id: setup
      activity: setup
      input:
        agentId: "{{params.agentId}}"
        setup:
          - cmd: "mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills && cp -rn \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/. ~/.claude/skills/"
          - cmd: "if [ -f $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md ]; then bash \"${H_SKILLS_DIR:?H_SKILLS_DIR must be set to the h skills root}\"/install-steering.sh $AGENT_APP_DIR/steering/h-runtime.md; fi"
    - id: plan
      activity: "{{params.runActivity}}"
      input:
        outputContract: {"properties":{"plan":{"description":"the implementation plan, self-contained and grounded in the code actually read — the artifact a downstream reviewer or implementer consumes","type":"string"},"skipped":{"description":"present when no real planning was possible — e.g. the change already appears implemented; omitted otherwise","type":"string"}},"required":["plan"],"type":"object"}
        cwd: "{{worktree.worktreePath}}"
        model: "{{params.modelPlan}}"
        permissionMode: plan
        task: |-
          You are in a git worktree of the target repository, on branch feature/{{params.slug}}.
  
          Investigate the request under ===SPEC=== below and produce an implementation plan.
          Ground it in the code you actually read — cite real paths and real existing symbols,
          and follow the conventions of the nearest precedent already in the tree. Do NOT write
          code or modify any files: this run plans only, and a separate run implements.
  
          Your plan is consumed by another agent as its sole spec, so it must stand alone —
          name the files to change, what to add or alter in each, and the tests that prove the
          acceptance criteria. If the change already appears implemented, say so in `skipped`
          and keep `plan` to what you found.
          
          ===OUTPUT CONTRACT===
          End your final message with a fenced ```json code block containing a single JSON
          object matching this schema. The block is machine-validated: a missing or
          mismatching block fails this step. Nothing may follow the block.
          {
            "properties": {
              "plan": {
                "description": "the implementation plan, self-contained and grounded in the code actually read — the artifact a downstream reviewer or implementer consumes",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "skipped": {
                "description": "present when no real planning was possible — e.g. the change already appears implemented; omitted otherwise",
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "plan"
            ],
            "type": "object"
          }
  
          ===SPEC===
          {{params.spec}}
  outputs:
    type: object
    required:
      - plan
    properties:
      plan:
        type: string
        description: >-
          the implementation plan, self-contained and grounded in the code actually read —
          the artifact a downstream reviewer or implementer consumes
      skipped:
        type: string
        description: >-
          present when no real planning was possible — e.g. the change already appears
          implemented; omitted otherwise
  panelSynthesis: |-
    Merge the panelists' plans into ONE implementation plan. Prefer the plan that is better
    grounded in the code actually read over the one that merely sounds thorough, and merge
    complementary steps rather than picking a side when they compose. Where they disagree on
    an approach, choose one, state briefly why in the plan itself, and make sure the result is
    a single coherent sequence an implementer can follow start to finish.
  
  '''
